# Two branches that each drop or add an entry next to the other's merge without a conflict:
# `union` keeps both sides' lines. A line one side dropped can come back that way, and the ratchet
# then names it (a `fails` entry that passes, or one listed twice), so a merge can't loosen the list
# silently, except for a `builder` entry, which leaves its test out of the run (`docs/tooling/ci.md`
# § Windows lane).
ci-known-failures.tsv merge=union
